WHAT: Raises object helper inlining limits for cross-function scalarization.
max_multi_use_object_helper_insts: 14→24, call_count threshold adjusted.

WHY: Object helper functions (struct constructors, field accessors) that cross
function boundaries prevent scalarization. Raising limits allows more of these
to be inlined, enabling the optimizer to eliminate intermediate obj.alloc/store/load.

GAS IMPACT: None on any contract.

TEAM NOTES: The remaining struct-passing overhead is architectural, not a
threshold problem. Small structs like G1Point{x,y} go through objref parameters
regardless of inlining limits. The fix requires SSA aggregate representation
(ExtractValue/InsertValue) in Sonatina's EVM codegen.
